+/// The face-decode failures a partial element may carry (RE-224 admission):
+/// a face whose surface pointer or UV boundary did not resolve, a trimmed face
+/// past its triangle budget, or a surface sampled outside its envelope. A
+/// trimmed face that needs a finer interior lattice is not among them: on the
+/// public reference models the only partial meshes that passed the count rule were
+/// sanitary terminals whose one such face was not Revit's body, so they stay
+/// boxed.
+const PARTIAL_FACE_FAILURES: [&str; 4] = [
+    "missing surface pointer target",
+    "disconnected UV boundary",
+    "trimmed face exceeds its budget",
+    "surface coordinates outside envelope",
